OL,3,ADame Jenni Murray died days after car
OL,4,Acrash, inquest hears
OL,5,
OL,6,FBBC broadcaster Dame Jenni Murray died
OL,7,Fdays after being involved in a car
OL,8,Fcrash in which she was dazzled by
OL,9,Fheadlights, an inquest was told.
OL,11,FDame Jenni, who was the longest-serving
OL,12,Fpresenter of BBC Radio 4's Woman's
OL,13,FHour, died aged 75 on 12 March, eight
OL,14,Fdays after a collision in north London.
OL,16,FNorth London area coroner Tony Murphy
OL,17,Fruled her cause of death was
OL,18,Fbronchopneumonia caused by fractures to
OL,19,Fher rib and sternum fractures sustained
OL,20,Fin the crash.
OL,23,APub: 27-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,162,160,200,105,0,100
